[SF3b the negative, CONSTRUCTIVELY — round-1 MINOR 2]
  The pin declared a completion count > 1 'RIGOROUS in the
  negative'.  That is not automatic: a kernel of the
  linearization exhibits a nearby SOLUTION only at a regular
  point of the (quadratic) variety, and the receipt never argued
  regularity.  The stronger fact is true and cheap, and is
  certified here: SOME kernel directions generate an exact LINE
  inside the variety — and not all do, which is precisely round
  1's point.  Along b* + t.v with v in the kernel, F(b*+t.v) =
  t^2.Q(v), so the line lies in the variety iff Q(v) = 0; the
  kernel basis is SEARCHED for such a v.  The COUNT of qualifying
  basis vectors is BASIS-DEPENDENT (the RREF basis follows the
  terminal-class ordering) and is deliberately not reported as a
  number; the two facts below are basis-free.
  Vanishing at four distinct t (0, 1, 1/3, 2) then makes the
  quadratic identically zero — no numerics, no regularity
  assumption.
